<title>CANADA: Goodale has no comment on Canada rail rate request.</title>
<headline>Goodale has no comment on Canada rail rate request.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Minister Ralph Goodale declined to comment on Tuesday on an appeal by Canada's largest grain handler against a decision that cut a rail rate discount.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan Wheat Pool asked the cabinet on Monday to rescind a decision by the Canadian Transportation Agency which, it said, effectively raised the maximum freight rate scale for grain to C$0.40 a tonne from C$0.30.</p>
<p>The decision pertained to the calculation of the railways' cost of capital.</p>
<p>Goodale told reporters he was unable to comment on a matter that was subject to a formal appeal.</p>
<p>((Randall Palmer, Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
